WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Today: how plants turn light into food.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Photosynthesis happens in the chloroplasts of leaf cells.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Chlorophyll absorbs red and blue light and reflects green.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.000
That is why leaves look green to us.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:21.000
The oxygen we breathe comes from splitting water, not from carbon dioxide.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:56.000
The sugar is built in the Calvin cycle, which does not need light.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:46.000
Next week: how plants breathe at night.
